{
  "name": "D3 interactive widget + skill",
  "overview": "Add per-post opt-in D3 support to the Jekyll/Distill blog, build an interactive Binomial-to-Poisson convergence widget (n slider + presets) below the existing static figure in the CTMC post, then capture the learnings as a project-local skill.",
  "plan": "# D3 Interactive Widget for Distill Posts\n\n## Decisions (confirmed)\n- Keep the static three-panel TikZ figure; add the interactive widget after it as a separate figure.\n- Controls: `n` slider only (lambda fixed at 3), plus preset buttons for n = 10 / 50 / 200.\n- D3 adopted site-wide as the interactive-figure library, opt-in per post like `tikzjax: true`.\n\n## 1. D3 loader include\n- New [_includes/scripts/d3.html](_includes/scripts/d3.html), mirroring [_includes/scripts/tikzjax.html](_includes/scripts/tikzjax.html):\n  - `{% if page.d3 %}` guard, load D3 v7 UMD bundle from jsDelivr with `defer` (global `d3`).\n- Add `{% include scripts/d3.html %}` in [_includes/head.html](_includes/head.html) next to the tikzjax include.\n\n## 2. Reusable JS helpers\n- New `assets/js/stochviz/` directory (small, grows with future posts):\n  - `distributions.js` — `binomialPmf(n, p, k)`, `poissonPmf(lambda, k)` (log-space for large n to avoid overflow).\n  - `pmf-widget.js` — a `createPmfConvergenceWidget(container, opts)` function: renders SVG axes, blue binomial bars, red Poisson dots, and wires the slider/preset buttons; redraws bars on input. Reads colors from CSS custom properties so dark mode works.\n- Loaded from the post with two plain `\u003cscript src=...\u003e` tags (no bundler).\n\n## 3. Styles\n- In [_sass/_distill.scss](_sass/_distill.scss): add a `.stochviz-panel` card (same look as `.tikz-panel` but background from theme variables since D3 draws with CSS colors), plus styles for the control row (slider, value readout, preset buttons).\n- If needed, add `--stochviz-*` color variables to [_sass/_themes.scss](_sass/_themes.scss) for light/dark (bar fill/stroke, reference-dot red, axis gray).\n\n## 4. Embed in the CTMC post\n- In [_posts/2026-05-10-ctmc.md](_posts/2026-05-10-ctmc.md):\n  - Add `d3: true` to front matter.\n  - After the existing Figure 1 `\u003cd-figure\u003e` (ends ~line 197), add a new `\u003cd-figure\u003e` with the widget container, controls, `\u003cfigcaption\u003e` (Figure 2), and the two script tags + init call.\n  - One bridging sentence in prose inviting the reader to drag `n`.\n- No renumbering needed (no later numbered figures in the post).\n\n## 5. Verify\n- Jekyll serve with drafts is already running (terminal 1); confirm the page builds and the rendered HTML contains the D3 script and widget markup (curl the post URL). Check for console-visible issues by reviewing the generated markup; user visually confirms slider behavior in browser.\n- Check both light and dark themes use readable colors (CSS vars, not hardcoded).\n\n## 6. Project-local skill (last step)\n- After implementation, write `.cursor/skills/distill-d3-widget/SKILL.md` modeled on [.cursor/skills/distill-tikz/SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/distill-tikz/SKILL.md):\n  - Frontmatter (name, description, trigger conditions), site wiring table (`d3: true`, loader include, `assets/js/stochviz/`, scss), embed template, helper API reference, styling/dark-mode rules, gotchas learned during implementation (KaTeX interplay, Kramdown + script tags, distill grid columns), and a checklist.\n  - Reference the CTMC post widget as the worked example.",
